// Copy to StravaSecrets.xcconfig (gitignored) and fill in your own Strava OAuth app's values.
// Register a free API application at https://www.strava.com/settings/api.
//
// IMPORTANT — Authorization Callback Domain: set it to exactly
//     localhost
// Strava validates the redirect_uri's HOST against this domain and only whitelists localhost /
// 127.0.0.1 regardless of scheme, so NOOP uses noop://localhost (below). The redirect is caught by
// NOOP's already-registered `noop` URL scheme — nothing ever binds a real loopback socket.
//
// Creating this file is ALSO what compiles the Strava import lane in: the compilation condition
// below gates every file in Strand/Strava/ (see StravaConfig.xcconfig). Without this file, a build
// contains zero Strava network code — "fully offline" stays a byte-level property of the binary.
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) STRAVA_CLOUD_IMPORT
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID = your_numeric_client_id_here
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET = your_client_secret_here
// .xcconfig treats // as a start-of-comment ANYWHERE on the line (not just at line-start), so a
// literal "noop://localhost" here gets silently truncated to "noop:" — the empty macro expansion
// $() below breaks up the "//" token without changing the resolved string, which is still exactly
// noop://localhost at build time. Keep this trick if you edit the value.
STRAVA_REDIRECT_URI = noop:/$()/localhost
